  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, thanks for reaching out. I want to make sure I fix the right problem, so could you tell me a bit more? Specifically: what happens on your laptop (freezing, slow apps, a error message, a crash or blue screen, a printer or Teams issue), when it started, and whether anything changed around that time, such as an update or a new app. Also, please do a full restart of your laptop (Start, Power, Restart, not just closing the lid) and make sure it is connected to the network, then reply with what you see. I've checked your laptop: disk space is fine, but it hasn't checked in with us for 12 days, so a restart and connection should help us get a clear reading.",
  "internal_note": "Sender Sofia Rossi (user 7, Marketing, America/New_York, usual hours 09:00-17:00). Account active, no failed logins, not blocked, password set 2026-09-11, VPN enabled. Mailbox 27.9% used. Only device BL-LT-0107 (Windows 11 Pro): offline, last check-in 2026-09-29 03:12 UTC, warning 'No check-in for 12 days', disk 140 GB free of 256 GB (54.7%). Ticket text is too vague to identify the symptom ('the thing again'). Did not run sign-in, MFA, or quarantine checks since nothing points to account or security issues. No fix applied. Next step: get symptom details and whether the laptop was restarted or off; re-check device status once it is online. Follow KB-019 (slow/freezing) if symptoms match; KB-022/KB-025 if printer or Teams. Escalate to Tier 2 if repeated crashes or blue screens persist after restart, or if the device stays offline.",
